  "required_actual_evidence_before_qualification": [
    "Native runner and daemon architecture must both be ARM64/aarch64 with Linux OSType; do not install or use foreign-architecture binfmt/QEMU for this qualification.",
    "Materialize exact Synapse and builder manifest digests in a separate preparation phase. Verify ImageID=config digest, complete layer identities, labels and platform. Qualification uses already materialized images with pull disabled.",
    "Record actual rustc -Vv host aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu, release 1.96.0 and commit ac68faa20c58cbccd01ee7208bf3b6e93a7d7f96; cargo/rustdoc, resolved compiler binaries, full rust sysroot and native linker/include/library inputs need immutable hashes.",
    "A base image label or Env alone does not prove the executed compiler or dynamic ELF library closure. Retain actual build commands, resolved tools, kernel/container runtime, executable bytes and before/after source/config/lock inventories.",
    "Record actual Docker/runner versions, available memory, free disk before prep/build/run, materialized image sizes and build-target growth. The 14 GB documentation figure is not a promise of unused space; compressed layer totals do not bound extracted/build size.",
    "Keep existing encrypted sync, isolation, independent dual agentd/matrixd, restart, outbox/dedup and external delivery assertions. Retain all failures and original required test names; host-specific evidence adapter cannot relax business assertions.",
    "No runtime network fetch or tool installation may silently change a sealed sysroot/tool manifest. Any added preparation tooling needs exact source/version/digest and the resulting image or filesystem inventory."
  ],
